    "case_id": "amb1-case01-product-scope",
    "focal_region": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 5 USER]\ne040\tThere is another complication.\ne041\tLina is excited, but she is also one of two people carrying on-call, and the last incident hit her hard.\ne042\tShe says the reporting work would give her energy.\ne043\tOur infrastructure engineer says that is exactly how we keep avoiding the boring work until it becomes an emergency.\ne044\tI can see both sides.\ne045\tForcing Lina onto reliability because it is responsible might burn her out; letting her chase the new layer might leave everyone else holding the risk.\n[Turn 5 ASSISTANT]\ne046\tThat makes this partly a sequencing and ownership question, not only feature selection.\ne047\tLina's energy is a real resource, but it should not make the reliability burden disappear for other people.\ne048\tOne possible design is to time-box her investigation while another owner defines the minimum reliability work that cannot slip, then reconvene with actual effort and ownership.\ne049\tBut if the team cannot staff both without wishful allocation, the experiment will not solve the conflict; it will merely postpone naming it.\n[Turn 6 USER]\ne050\tNorthline emailed this morning.\ne051\tThey can live with their manual CSV process for another quarter, although their operations lead may move to a different role by then.\ne052\tThat reduces the urgency, but it also means we could lose the person who understands the problem best.\ne053\tOur smaller customers are not asking for reporting.\ne054\tThey are asking for fewer confusing states and faster support.\ne055\tI am less sure this is a broad product signal than I was yesterday, but more sure the discovery could be valuable.\n[Turn 6 ASSISTANT]\ne056\tThe new email separates two clocks: delivery can wait, but access to a knowledgeable collaborator may not.\ne057\tThat supports a narrower move—capture the workflow and test the reusable concept now without beginning full implementation.\ne058\tIt also strengthens the case for protecting the smaller-customer and reliability commitments, since their demand is current and repeated.\ne059\tThe open question is whether your team can conduct discovery without it becoming an unofficial project through momentum alone.",
